D. Proof-route synthesis
  The S677 primitive apex-debt branch is not one phenomenon.  It splits into local opening modes.  Clock shutter covers rows whose deleted-apex unit-clock cone outlives the apex collar.  Rows not caught there still expose endpoint-owner intervals: an apex-free side door, a one-apex hinge, or a pure apex-period aperture.

  Lemma package suggested by the audit:
    L1 clock shutter: deleted-apex cone width > 1/(14a) opens p0.
    L2 side door: a safe interval with non-apex owners on both ends survives apex debt.
    L3 hinge: one apex owner plus one non-apex owner gives a transversal opening.
    L4 aperture: two apex endpoints still leave an apex-period gap if non-apex depth is zero.

  This is the owner-private deletion idea in a usable form: do not ask whether the apex is globally harmless.  Ask which boundary of a specific safe interval it owns.
